ich  reflected my convictions a pro-european  speech but in which there was an attempt  to find the solutions to the divisions  that exist between west and east and  south and north giving me confidence in  advance that I bridge the divisions we  do see definitely and that is what I  want to do I want to unite Europe I want  to bring Europe forward and if we want  to be successful in Europe we have to  stand together of course we will always  have differences of course we will  always have issues but we have to focus  on the big topics on the big questions  and that's my task Thomas Meyer Thomas  Meyer from standard for concerns  president in symphonies actor C  president designation you've said gee  you want to come to Cal with the  Parliament work hand in hand he said  that during your speech  what do you think about this  specifically your main thing first there  will be to put the Commission together  and to draw up a working program  personally do you want to bring the  Parliament into play in setting out the  working program what would that mean  specifically in terms of work bringing  together the heads of the the group  could that be perhaps difficult bringing  them in and getting them to work  alongside you  well the basic lines are in the  political guidelines and blind lines  they're very clear they need to be  worked and further over the last two  weeks I've worked very closely with with  everybody I needed to get to know people  to start off with I needed to look at  the different priorities and compare  them and see how they fitted in with my  convictions  and where we can move ahead together I  think it is a very important task in  this Parliament to be very transparent  to be very open to work very closely in  intensively alongside  political groups my parliamentary  experiences the more open you are the  closer you are to people the better your  work will be in difficult issues where  you need to work together and make  progress there where it's ver